<title>CHINA: Shanghai steel mill goes into operation.</title>
<headline>Shanghai steel mill goes into operation.</headline>
<dateline>SHANGHAI 1997-07-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Shanghai Yichang Tin-plated Steel Sheet Mill, with an investment of 410 million yuan ($49 million), began operations on Friday, Xinhua news agency said.</p>
<p>The mill was one of Shanghai's key industrial projects, designed to ease a national shortage of tin-plated steel sheets and reduce the need for imports, Xinhua said, without further details.</p>
<p>($1=8.3 yuan)</p>
<p>-- Shanghai Newsroom (8621) 6279-7004</p>
